// Example from: Docs/03-language-basics/loops-and-iteration.md
// The step is a distance, so a negative step is always reported. This range
// is empty in the written direction, so the loop runs zero times and the
// program carries on, with a warning on stderr naming the loop it meant.

count from 5 to 1 by -1:
    display count
end count
display "The program carries on."
